from lb import e
E=[
e("Book 2 - Summary (Sky Scar Lake and the Legacy of the Reaper)",["Book 2","Legacy of the Reaper","City of Fallen Echoes","Sky Scar Lake","Order of the Reaper trials","Star Seed arc"],
"""BOOK 2: Jason confronts Elspeth Arella, wins Sophie's six-month indenture at a hearing and makes her an adventurer (Swift, Balance, Wind -> Mystic confluence; Iron rank). Belinda joins as Clive's research assistant, later Charlatan confluence (Magic, Trap, Adept). A Continental Council inquiry (Tabitha Gert) demotes Jason to one star and Danielle/Humphrey to two. Star-seed Builder cultists are exposed: Jonah Geller dies when the Purity archbishop tries to purge a star seed; Thadwick's seed is extracted; Timos, a Builder cultist, recruits Thadwick. Jason forms a team with Humphrey, Clive, Sophie and Neil Davone (Prosperity confluence). Emir Bahadir stages a contest for the Scythe of the Reaper in the Order of the Reaper's hidden astral space under Sky Scar Lake: the City of Fallen Echoes with five Legacy trials (courage, intellect, resolve, capability, wisdom) and a hidden sixth insight trial. Jason takes the real Scythe, gets the Reaper Token and Shade (Shadow of the Reaper familiar) and Gordon (Avatar of Doom). Teammates' racial gifts transfigure. Cole Silva schemes. Jason meets Zara Rimaros. Jason receives the Godless Prophet title. Emir gives the team a Cloud Palace; Jason binds a Cloud Flask and houseboat. The book ends with a raid on a Builder island camp where Rufus unleashes Kingdom of Eclipse; Timos and Thadwick escape.""",2),
e("Tabitha Gert and the Continental Council Inquiry",["Tabitha Gert","Continental Council","inquiry team","Gert"],
"""Tabitha Gert: strict rule-following Adventure Society official (black pin) who leads the Continental Council inquiry into the Greenstone expedition disaster. Demotes Jason to one star (Cassandra Mercer then breaks off their relationship, 'We end here'), demotes Danielle and Humphrey to two stars, expels the Phael family from the Society, and serves as interim Greenstone director. Believes rules are the basis of civilisation.""",2),
e("Star Seeds and the Builder's Plan",["Star Seed","star seeds","Builder's plan","Timos","Builder cultist","Builder cult"],
"""Star seeds: hair-thin metal-wire implants (nucleus like a hulled coconut) made by great astral beings (here the Builder) that puppet the host, transform them into flesh-steel abominations and explode into crystal if the host talks. The Builder wants to sever astral spaces from the world and hold them intact to build its own world (cataclysmic for the planet). Timos is a long-embedded cultist in Greenstone (kills Frank the tunnel worker). Five star-seed hosts (Jonah Geller, Thadwick Mercer and three others) were used as decoys; Jonah dies in a Purity purge, Thadwick survives extraction. Builder cultists summoned Jason by accident while trying to summon a Clockwork King. The Church of Purity quietly tolerates the cult via a wider accord, and Archbishop Nicolas Hendren/Herston is complicit.""",2),
e("The Builder (original)",["Builder","The Builder","Clockwork King","Clockwork Kings","Builder cult","world engineer golem"],
"""The Builder (original): a great astral being obsessed with physical reality it cannot share; builds its own world out of stolen astral spaces; recruits cults with gifts of power, uses star seeds and constructs (golems, clockwork animals). Native gold-rank Clockwork Kings of the Builder's world are dragon-like leaders. The Builder's cult attacked Cyrion in the past (world engineer golems left outside the walls). In Book 3 Jason confronts and sanctions it; the Builder's role passes to a messenger (the new Builder). See Book 3 for details.""",2),
e("Order of the Reaper",["Order of the Reaper","Order of Reaper","Scythe of the Reaper","Reaper's order","Legacy trials"],
"""Order of the Reaper: ancient royal assassins (knife in the dark for mad rulers) and hunters of undead/necromancers, accepted by nations and churches until the church of the Unliving and Purity, in an unholy compact, destroyed it. Churches also bargained with vorger (deep-astral entities) to turn fleeing initiates into flesh abominations. The last grandmaster (an outworlder with dark essence) hid survivors and the Legacy of the Reaper in a proto-astral space (the City of Fallen Echoes) under Sky Scar Lake, with trials open 18 days and iron-rank entry only. The hidden insight trial reveals the Order survives as a quiet volunteer network matching tasks to people of conscience; the trials are recruitment bait. The real Scythe of the Reaper (silver blade, gold shaft, obsidian inlay; diamond-rank, enormously heavy) is delivered to Emir Bahadir by Jason. The Way of the Reaper martial art comes from the Order.""",2),
e("City of Fallen Echoes",["City of Fallen Echoes","Fallen Echoes","Legacy of the Reaper contest","Sky Scar Lake"],
"""City of Fallen Echoes: ancient circular overgrown city in an astral space (12 gate towers; sea around) entered through Sky Scar Lake's drowned fortress. Trials: choose wisdom or courage first (wisdom gives Medallion of Escape + Lesser Miracle Potion); city traversal (capability); nightmare-hag courage test (Jason faces an evil future self; Humphrey his family); intellect constellation puzzle (reward Summoner's Die: Form); resolve (refuse to execute captive priests; reward Immortal Crest); hidden insight trial. Monsters: siege golems, margolls, sloth demon, grizzards, vorger swarms, flesh abominations, blood root vine (killed by Jason, Jory, Beth and others). 19 adventurers pass all trials; ~419 time-displaced priests and holy warriors are freed. The astral space is at gold monster density mostly iron, some bronze.""",2),
e("Shade (Shadow of the Reaper)",["Shade","Shadow of the Reaper","Shade familiar"],
"""Shade: British-sounding living silhouette, invigilator of the Legacy trials and a fragment of the Reaper's shadow (also familiar of the grandmaster); becomes Jason's Dark familiar via the Awakening Stone of the Reaper ('Shadow of the Reaper', later Shadow of the Hegemon). Incorporeal, up to three bodies (later 211), hides in other people's shadows, drains mana by touch, lets Jason see through bodies. Polite, dry, indispensable; pilots Jason's ships and acts as butler. 'The laws of physics are strong suggestions.' In Book 11 Shade sanctions himself becoming the Shadow of the Hegemon.""",2),
e("Gordon (Avatar of Doom)",["Gordon","Avatar of Doom","Jason's doom familiar"],
"""Gordon: Jason's Doom familiar (Avatar of Doom). Appears as a nebula eye (orange eye, blue iris) in a dark cloak with two orbiting eye-orbs (blue-in-orange, orange-in-blue); communicates yes/no by orbs; orange orb fires resonating-force, blue orb disruptive-force beams; afflicts Vulnerable; can subsume into Jason's aura to mask or strengthen it. Chant: 'When worlds end, you are the arbiter... I have doom to bring.' At gold: butterflies create affliction clouds; Harbinger of Doom spreads afflictions.""",2),
e("Reaper Token and Racial Gift Transfiguration",["Reaper Token","Transfiguration","racial gift","gift evolution","Hero's Drive","Thirst for Knowledge","Life Guard","Mana Wellspring","Attack of the Mirage Dragon","Tactical Map"],
"""Astral blessing tokens (like Jason's Reaper Token) trigger racial-gift evolution. After the Legacy contest: Jason's Map -> Tactical Map; Clive's Human Ambition -> Thirst for Knowledge; Neil's Life Affinity -> Life Guard; Sophie's Mana Integrity -> Mana Wellspring; Humphrey's Special Attack Affinity -> Attack of the Mirage Dragon (illusory double of special attacks); Stash is revealed as a rare Mirage Dragon. Jason's Mysterious Stranger became Dark Rider. Gifts are tailored to the soul. Awakening Stone of the Reaper (unranked legendary, one per adventurer who reached the tower) awakens Reaper-themed abilities: Jason Shadow of the Reaper, Hand of the Reaper and Avatar of Doom; Neil Hero's Moment and Reaper's Redoubt; Humphrey Spirit Reaper and Immortality; Sophie Deny the Reaper.""",2),
e("Godless Prophet (title) and Gods' thanks",["Godless Prophet","title","gods thanked Jason","Dominion Healer thank"],
"""After Jason frees the time-displaced priests and holy warriors, the Healer, Dominion and other gods appear in the priest camp to thank him; the pressure alters his aura and grants the title Godless Prophet (aura gains an echo of transcendent power). Stash, shapeshifted as Jason, caused a streaking incident.""",2),
e("Zara Rimaros (Hurricane Princess)",["Zara","Zara Rimaros","Zara Nareen","Hurricane Princess","Storm Princess"],
"""Zara Rimaros: celestine princess (caramel skin, sapphire eyes, waterfall-blue Rimaros royal-line hair) of the Storm Kingdom (Rimaros), former 'Hurricane Princess'. Meets Jason when he teleports into her tent (he offers gem-berry and milk-nut squares); gives only 'Zara'. Aunt Vesper Rimaros. Disgraced by a series of mistakes, she adventured as Zara Nareen with Orin's team then Jason's; storm/wind area attacks later concentrated into fist-sized storms. Romantic tension with Jason grows (Book 12: she restores her sapphire hair, resumes her princess role, wants the Storm Kingdom to abolish indenture). In Book 2 she is iron-rank. See Rimaros entries.""",2),
e("Valdis Volaire",["Valdis","Valdis Volaire","Prince Valdis","Kingdom of Mirrors"],
"""Valdis Volaire: slight blond prince of the Kingdom of Mirrors (ruled eight centuries by the diamond-ranker the Mirror King, Victor Volaire; Valdis is son of the queen consort). Essences sword, swift, adept, master; dimensional jacket, expensive gear; dueling-obsessed. Joins Clive's team in Fallen Echoes. Challenges everyone aboard Jason's ship to duels in Book 12.""",2),
e("Neil Davone (Prosperity)",["Prosperity","Neil's powers","Chrysalis Golem","Reels of Fortune","Spoils of Victory"],
"""Neil Davone: elf (chubby for an elf, muscular under clothes) of the Davone family of Greenstone's Island. Essences shield, growth, renewal -> Prosperity confluence: healing, cleansing, Burst Shield, Absorbing Shield, buffs (Giant's Might, Armour of Renewal), Fountain of Life, Bolster, Reels of Fortune (random effects), Spoils of Victory (aura), Chrysalis Golem summon, Hero's Moment, Reaper's Redoubt, Life Guard. Joins Jason after Jason invites him ('honest foot forward'). Crushed on Cassandra Mercer.""",2),
e("Humphrey's Team / Early Team Biscuit",["Humphrey's team","Team Biscuit","Biscuit","team composition"],
"""Team formed late Book 2: Jason (dark/blood/sin/doom), Humphrey (might, magic, wing, dragon), Clive (magic, rune, balance, karmic), Sophie (swift, wind, balance, mystic), Neil (shield, growth, renewal, prosperity), later Belinda (magic, trap, adept, charlatan), Zara and others. Tactic: buff Humphrey with Clive and Neil and let him go; Clive and Neil act as bait. Jason's biscuits give the team its name. Beth Cavendish's and Rick Geller's teams are rivals in the mirage chamber.""",2),
e("Sophie Wexler's Abilities",["Sophie's abilities","Free Runner","Mirage Step","Cloud Step","Between the Raindrops","Eternal Moment","Moment of Oneness","Deny the Reaper"],
"""Sophie's 20 abilities (Swift/Balance/Wind/Mystic): Free Runner, Avatar of Speed, Between the Raindrops, Alacrity's Reward, Eternal Moment (Swift); Equilibrium, Cloud Step, Moment of Oneness, Karmic Warrior, Deny the Reaper (Balance); Wind Blade, Cleansing Breeze (aura), Leaf on the Wind, Wind Wave, Child of the Celestial Wind (Wind); Strong Soul, Sight Beyond Sight, Immortal Fist, Radiant Fist, Mirage Step (Mystic). Racial gift Mana Wellspring. Wields Siege Grips; unarmed 'empty hand' skill better than Rufus's.""",2),
e("Belinda Callahan's Abilities",["Belinda's abilities","Bag of Tricks","Echo Spirit","Astral Lantern","Instant Adept","Counterfeit Combatant","Specious Sorcerer","Power Thief","Shimmer","Gemini"],
"""Belinda's essences: Magic (Bag of Tricks, Power Thief, spell mimicry, Astral Lantern), Trap (Bait and Switch, rune trap, pit trap, tethers/Force Tether), Adept (Blessing of Readiness, cooldown aura, Instant Adept), Charlatan confluence (Echo Spirit, Beside Myself, Unexpected Allies, Counterfeit Combatant, Specious Sorcerer). Familiars: Shimmer (astral lantern: disruptive bolts, negates projectiles) and Gemini (echo spirit: mimics forms, switch-teleport). Gifts: Adventurer's Tools, Quick Learner, The Price of Power, Face in the Crowd, Form and Function.""",2),
e("Jason's Cloud Palace, Cloud Flask and Houseboat",["Cloud Flask","cloud palace","Cloud House","houseboat","Cloud ship"],
"""Emir awards the winning team a bonded Cloud Palace (a growth item; Jason chosen as bonded owner); Jason binds a Cloud Flask (iron legendary growth item, soul-bound; adaptive; grows with bronze air/water and dimension quintessence) and summons an adaptive three-storey houseboat at Marina North, Greenstone. Over time it becomes his huge cloud ship (cruise-ship size, can shift into configurations like D20 icosahedron with eye-panels, a floating cloud palace, a passenger ship, a temple of Jason).""",2),
e("Immortal Crest (Soul Crest) and Tilly",["Immortal Crest","Soul Crest","tattoo","Tilly","tattooist"],
"""Soul crest: tattoo on the soul showing on the body; unique permanent ID verified worldwide by the Adventure Society; form reflects true nature. Tilly (old, wiry, no aura; knew young Emir, Gabriel and Arabelle) applies them in Jayapura. Jason's crest: a dark empty cloak under a silver-starred night with an open blue sky and golden sun at chest, 'the day hidden in the night'. Magical tattoos last until next rank (iron tattoos: burst recovery, DR burst, cooldown reduction, affliction-resistance reduction for Jason).""",2),
e("Rufus Remore - Kingdom of Eclipse",["Kingdom of Eclipse","Rufus's sun and moon swords","eclipse beam"],
"""Rufus's extra powers: golden sun sword leaves burning sun orbs; silver moon sword leaves chilling moons; after-image chain teleports; speed of light; ultimate Kingdom of Eclipse (chant 'Darkness and light, sun and moon...') firing an eclipse orb transcendent beam. At the end of Book 2 he uses it on the silver-rank abomination that killed Farrah in the Builder island raid, killing dozens but not it, and collapses.""",2),
e("Mirror King and Kingdom of Mirrors",["Mirror King","Victor Volaire","Kingdom of Mirrors","Calute"],
"""Mirror King (Victor Volaire): diamond-ranker ruling a small rich Kingdom of Mirrors for ~800 years; father of Valdis. Friend and ally of Roland Remore; rules via mirror domain. Mentioned again Book 12 as having tea with Roland.""",2),
e("Cole Silva schemes (Killian Laurent)",["Killian Laurent","Cole Silva schemes","Timos Builder"],
"""After Sophie slips beyond reach, Cole Silva kills a thug and hires Killian Laurent (sickly elf with 'particular appetites') to find a silver-rank adventurer who will quietly take Sophie and kill Jason; someone offers hidden help. The Builder cult's Timos recruits Thadwick Mercer (now a puppet-in-waiting).""",2),
e("Hester Maharala",["Hester","Hester Maharala","Jayapura","Pranay"],
"""Hester Maharala: silver portal-user of Emir's staff, from Jayapura (large northern port of Pranay, a Sri Lanka-like landmass; world lacks Arabia so the Mediterranean joins the Indian Ocean). Mother Anise; family lifted by essences/cores. Jayapura has float discs, glowing-frame airships, Mystic Quarter, and the Mirage Chamber Association leagues for iron/bronze/silver (no gold division; pros avoid cores near silver). She can portal to places she has visited; closest to the desert aperture is the city Boko.""",2),
e("Jory's Alchemical Abomination form",["Alchemical Abomination","Jory monster form","Lesser Miracle Potion","miracle potion"],
"""Lesser Miracle Potion: iron legendary alchemy that fully restores health/mana/stamina for normal/iron users. Jory finds its formula in the astral space and drinks mixed potions to become a patchwork super-strong 'Alchemical Abomination'; second form skinny and oily, dissolving vorger. His powers: Eldritch Eyes (orbs deliver potions), Potion Mystic, Universal Reagent.""",2),
e("Jason's Backstory (told to Cassandra)",["Jason backstory","Casselton","Casselton Educational Institute","Kaito","Amy"],
"""Jason grew up in a coastal tourist town (Casselton Beach) attending Casselton Educational Institute; mother in property sales, father a landscape architect; Japanese-heritage family. Older brother Kaito (socially chameleonic) and childhood sweetheart Amy (next door) later married, 'blew up my whole life'. He later worked assistant manager at a bulk office supplier ('Station-Eyrie' joke). Learned people fill gaps in stories. Gave worst-things quip about the town.""",2),
e("Mercer scandal and Thadwick's capture",["Thadwick captured","Timos threat","Beaufort Mercer","Crivens"],
"""Beaufort Mercer facilitated the Builder cult's escape through Hornis; Thalia (might, potent, swift, onslaught; silver) tipped Danielle. A clay-and-iron doppelganger 'Thadwick' appears at the Mercer manor with star-seed-controlled guards before the cult retakes him; Timos kills Frank.""",2),
e("Emir's Staff and Associates",["Callum Morse","Cal","Ketis","Greg","Amelia Hurin","William Hurin","Gabriel Remore","Arabelle Remore"],
"""Emir's old team: Emir, Gabriel Remore (gold; wind/fire sword dancer, dark curly hair), Arabelle Remore (Rufus's mother; rainbow-dyed hair; withering touch, urns of life force, healer), Callum 'Cal' Morse (gold stealth assassin, grizzled hunter). Ketis Bahadir is Emir's granddaughter (15, rainbow braids; learns the Way of the Reaper; her father died in the last monster surge). Amelia and William Hurin are Farrah's parents (bronze after Farrah's help). Staff nicknamed by shared first names ('Greg').""",2),
e("Awakening Stones - Reaper, Celestials, Karma and others",["Awakening Stone of the Reaper","Stone of the Celestials","Stone of Karma","Stone of Rebirth","Stone of the Avatar"],
"""Notable stones: Reaper (unranked legendary, 5 legendary stones awarded in Book 2), Celestials (created from an outworlder's ability; only 3 existed), Karma, Rebirth, Avatar, Rain (Sophie: Between the Raindrops), Moment (Sophie: Eternal Moment, Moment of Oneness), Preparation, Surge, Purgation (Cleansing Breeze), Sky (Leaf on the Wind). Divine stones (Inevitability, Persistence) from gods are revocable; astral-being gift stones are not. Jason refused Knowledge's 'poison pill' gifts: Divine Awakening Stone of Inevitability (aura Inevitable Demise), Soul-Purgation Tablet, Divine Awakening Stone of Persistence (spell Curse of Isolation).""",2),
]
